<!--
    ServiceNow Update Set record-definitions for the SERVICE PORTAL PAGE
    LAYOUT of the CASE STATUS LOOKUP page (`x_casemgmt_case_status`) inside
    the scoped application `x_casemgmt`.

    WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (the defect it closes)
    ...........................................
    Identical in cause to the sibling
    ./sp_page_layout_x_casemgmt_case_submit.xml: a Service Portal page
    renders only what its layout chain places on it -

        sp_page  <-  sp_container  <-  sp_row  <-  sp_column  <-  sp_instance
                                                                     |
                                                                     +-> sp_widget

    and this package shipped none of those four records. The status page
    therefore answered HTTP 200 anonymously and painted a blank viewport:
    no case-number input, no Look Up button, and - the user-visible
    consequence for AAP Validation Gate 5 - the verbatim not-found text
    "No case found with that number." never appeared on screen even though
    the endpoint returned it correctly. The lookup widget was healthy all
    along; it was embedded nowhere.

    WHAT IT AUTHORS (one record each, in dependency order)
    .....................................................
      1. sp_container  "Case Status Lookup - Container 1" -> parents to the page
      2. sp_row        row 1 of that container
      3. sp_column     full-width (size 12) column of that row
      4. sp_instance   places ../widgets/sp_widget_x_casemgmt_case_lookup_widget.xml
                       in that column

    One full-width widget matches AAP Section 0.4.4's description of Page 2 -
    "a single input (case number) and a result panel" - and the widget
    renders its own <h2>Case Status Lookup</h2> heading, so
    `sp_instance.title` is left EMPTY to avoid a duplicate heading.

    Field choices, reference-resolution rationale and the measured
    preview-resolution rule are documented in full in the sibling file
    ./sp_page_layout_x_casemgmt_case_submit.xml; they are identical here.

    THIS RECORD SET MUST LOAD AFTER:
      - ../../app/sys_app/x_casemgmt_case_management.xml  (the scope)
      - ../pages/sp_page_x_casemgmt_case_status.xml       (the parent page)
      - ../widgets/sp_widget_x_casemgmt_case_lookup_widget.xml (the widget
        placed here, which calls
        ../rest/sys_ws_definition_x_casemgmt_case_status_lookup.xml)

    VALIDATION-GATE MAPPING (AAP Section 0.7.3)
    ...........................................
      Gate 5 ("Portal - lookup"): "Status lookup returns correct data for
      valid case number - Correct status/subject/opened_date returned;
      'not found' message for invalid number." These four records are what
      let a human - rather than a curl command - see either outcome.

    DETERMINISTIC IDENTIFIERS
    .........................
    Every `sys_id` below is the MD5 of its own `sys_update_name`:
      sp_container_x_casemgmt_case_status         -> 7ec26735abd11959ba2b6a91190b42b2
      sp_row_x_casemgmt_case_status               -> b353f7cdd3a40c07dd8ed6a9393d38d4
      sp_column_x_casemgmt_case_status            -> 159071b339bfd27dcae48de4e32e4fb3
      sp_instance_x_casemgmt_case_lookup_widget   -> 5971ae890ee47d43b66ffbc8ca7f6eb4
    The referenced page (8881e418f5d24b17b641505a4f1dc814) and widget
    (e992deb0bd1657f36a38f5af6a46aeb2) sys_ids are the ones those two
    records already declare in this package.
-->
